  },
];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Reviews", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/reviews/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Aviron Treadmill", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/aviron-treadmill/" },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Does Aviron make a treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Yes. As of 20 October 2026 Aviron sells three treadmills in the US: the folding Justice ($1,999), the folding Podium ($2,499) and the non-folding Summit ($2,999), at Aviron’s sale prices with the 16-inch screen. Its earlier Victory treadmill is no longer listed on Aviron’s own store.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Can you use an Aviron treadmill without a membership?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Yes. Aviron says the membership is not required. Without it you keep the metrics screen, manual speed and incline, profiles, workout history and streaming apps such as Netflix and YouTube. The games, classes, scenic routes and competitions need the membership, and so does the 20-year warranty.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How much is the Aviron membership?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "On 20 October 2026 Aviron charged $29 a month billed annually ($348 a year), $34 a month month to month, or $2,499 once for a perpetual plan. Each extra Aviron machine adds $10 a month, or $999 on a perpetual plan, and one membership covers unlimited household profiles.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is the Aviron 20-year warranty real?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "It is real but conditional. Aviron’s terms require a purchase direct from its website, membership activation within 90 days and continued payment of a monthly or annual plan; perpetual plans do not qualify. Otherwise the warranty is 10 years on the frame and drive motor and one year on other parts, and it does not transfer.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What is the difference between the Aviron Justice, Podium and Summit?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "The Justice has a 3.5 CHP motor, 12.5 mph, 15% incline, a 20 by 59-inch deck and a 300 lb limit, and folds. The Podium has a 4.5 CHP motor, 14 mph, 18% incline, a 22 by 60-inch deck and a 350 lb limit, and also folds. The Summit adds a -6% to 42% grade range on a 22 by 61-inch deck, does not fold and weighs 364 lb.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Has the Aviron treadmill been recalled?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "We found no recall of any Aviron product when we searched the US Consumer Product Safety Commission’s recall database on 20 October 2026, and none in Health Canada’s listings. Register your treadmill with Aviron so you would be told of any future recall.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Can I use the Aviron app on another treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Not in any way we could confirm. Aviron’s standalone app launched in 2024 for Concept2 rowers, and we found no Aviron page listing a supported third-party treadmill. Some makers, including TKO, name Aviron as a compatible app, but confirm with Aviron before buying on that basis.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      description: description,
      author: { "@type": "Person", "@id": "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#shaheer-ali-khan", name: "Shaheer Ali Khan", honorificSuffix: "PhD", jobTitle: "Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist", url: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#who", sameAs: ["https://www.linkedin.com/in/shaheer-ali-khan-data/"], worksFor: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" } },
      datePublished: "2026-10-20",
      dateModified: "2026-10-20",
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" },
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      name: product.name,
      description: product.description,
      brand: { "@type": "Brand", name: product.name.split(" ")[0] },
      ...(product.priceBounds
        ? {
            offers: {
              "@type": "AggregateOffer",
              priceCurrency: "USD",
              lowPrice: product.priceBounds.low,
              highPrice: product.priceBounds.high,
              url: product.amazonUrl,
            },
          }
        : {}),
    })),
    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      name: title,
      numberOfItems: 3,
      itemListElement: PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => ({
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: index + 1,
        name: product.name,
        url: `https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/aviron-treadmill/#${product.id}`,
      })),
    },
  ],
};
---

<Layout
  title={`${title} | Treadmill Reviews USA`}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: "2026-10-20",
    modifiedTime: "2026-10-20",
    author: "Shaheer Ali Khan",
    section: "Fitness Equipment",
    tags: [
      "aviron treadmill",
      "aviron treadmill review",
      "aviron justice treadmill",
      "aviron podium treadmill",
      "aviron summit treadmill",
      "aviron victory treadmill",
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{ text: "Compare the Three Models", link: "#lineup" }}
>
  <article class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <div class="bg-gray-900 py-16 lg:py-24 relative overflow-hidden">
      <svg class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full opacity-10" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
        <pattern id="dot-pattern-avirontreadmill" x="0" y="0" width="24" height="24" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
          <circle cx="2" cy="2" r="1.5" fill="white"></circle>
        </pattern>
        <rect width="100%" height="100%" fill="url(#dot-pattern-avirontreadmill)"></rect>
      </svg>
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 relative z-10 text-center">
        <div class="flex justify-center mb-6">
          <TrustBadge />
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-3 mb-6 flex-wrap">
          <span class="bg-[#FF5A1F] text-white px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">
            Model Review
          </span>
          <span class="bg-green-500 text-white px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">
            Updated October 2026
          </span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-6xl font-black text-white leading-tight mb-8">
          Aviron Treadmill: <span class="text-[#5AA9FF]">Justice, Podium and Summit Reviewed</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
          Aviron is best known for its gamified rowers, but it does sell treadmills in the US: three of them since September 2026. This review sets out what the Justice, Podium and Summit cost, what Aviron and independent reviewers agree on, what the membership adds and what the machines do without it, and the conditions attached to the 20-year warranty.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4">
          <a href="#short-answer" class="bg-[#FF5A1F] hover:bg-[#E64F16] text-white px-8 py-4 rounded-xl font-black no-underline transition-colors uppercase tracking-widest text-sm">
            The Short Answer
          </a>
          <a href="#lineup" class="bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/20 text-white px-8 py-4 rounded-xl font-black no-underline transition-colors uppercase tracking-widest text-sm border border-white/20">
            Compare the Three Models
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>


    <!-- Author & Meta -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-12">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 py-8 border-b border-gray-100">
        <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD" width="48" height="48" class="w-12 h-12 rounded-full" />
        <div>
          <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 leading-tight"><a href="/editorial-standards/#who" rel="author" class="text-gray-900 no-underline hover:underline">Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD</a></p>
          <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm leading-tight">Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist · ACSM-EP, CSCS</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block w-px h-8 bg-gray-200"></div>
        <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm">
          Last Updated: <strong class="text-gray-700">October 20, 2026</strong>
        </p>
        <div class="ml-auto">
          <SocialProof users="1.6k" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="not-prose my-10 bg-blue-50 border border-blue-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 m-0 leading-relaxed">
          <strong class="text-gray-900">What we checked, and what we have not done.</strong> On
          20 October 2026 we read Aviron's US treadmill shop page, the product pages and technical
          specifications for the Justice, Podium and Summit, its membership, warranty and return-policy
          pages, its August 2026 launch and comparison posts and its 9 September 2026 press release.
          We cross-checked the figures against Garage Gym Reviews' hands-on reviews of all three
          models (updated 24 September, 7 October and 19 October 2026) and Wellworthy's launch
          coverage of 12 August 2026, and we searched the US Consumer Product Safety Commission's
          recall database for Aviron. Figures on the product cards are ones on which Aviron and at
          least one independent source agree; where they disagree, or where only Aviron gives a
          figure, we say so. We have not tested any Aviron treadmill, and none of the numbers here
          are our own measurements. Prices are those shown on avironactive.com on 20 October 2026
          and change often. As an Amazon Associate we earn from qualifying purchases.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>


    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-8">
      <div class="not-prose bg-orange-50 border border-orange-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-black text-gray-900 mt-0 mb-3">Our Top Picks</h2>
        <ul class="list-none m-0 p-0">
          <li class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-2 py-2 border-b border-orange-100 last:border-0">
            <span class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#FF5A1F]">Cheapest Aviron:</span>
            <a href="#aviron-justice" class="font-bold text-gray-900 no-underline hover:underline">Aviron Justice Treadmill</a>
            <a href="#aviron-justice" class="ml-auto text-xs font-bold text-[#0F62FE] no-underline hover:underline">Jump to review &darr;</a>
          </li>
          <li class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-2 py-2 border-b border-orange-100 last:border-0">
            <span class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#FF5A1F]">Most Buyers:</span>
            <a href="#aviron-podium" class="font-bold text-gray-900 no-underline hover:underline">Aviron Podium Treadmill</a>
            <a href="#aviron-podium" class="ml-auto text-xs font-bold text-[#0F62FE] no-underline hover:underline">Jump to review &darr;</a>
          </li>
          <li class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-2 py-2 border-b border-orange-100 last:border-0">
            <span class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#FF5A1F]">Steepest Incline:</span>
            <a href="#aviron-summit" class="font-bold text-gray-900 no-underline hover:underline">Aviron Summit Treadmill</a>
            <a href="#aviron-summit" class="ml-auto text-xs font-bold text-[#0F62FE] no-underline hover:underline">Jump to review &darr;</a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
      <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
        <h2 class="flex items-center gap-2 text-lg font-black text-gray-900 mt-0 mb-4">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-5 h-5 text-[#FF5A1F]" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4 6h16M4 12h16M4 18h7"></path></svg>
          In This Guide
        </h2>
        <nav class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2">
          <a href="#short-answer" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">1. Does Aviron Make a Treadmill? The Short Answer</a>
          <a href="#lineup" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">2. Justice vs Podium vs Summit</a>
          <a href="#victory" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">3. The Victory Treadmill</a>
          <a href="#cost" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">4. What It Costs</a>
          <a href="#membership" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">5. Membership and Free Features</a>
          <a href="#warranty-and-trial" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">6. Warranty and Returns</a>
          <a href="#summit-incline" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">7. The 42% Incline</a>
          <a href="#recalls-and-safety" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">8. Recalls and Safety</a>
          <a href="#space-and-setup" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">9. Space and Set-Up</a>
          <a href="#alternatives" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">10. Who Should Buy Something Else</a>
          <a href="#faq" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">11. Frequently Asked Questions</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          People searching for an Aviron treadmill are usually in one of two places: they own or
          have read about Aviron's rowing machine and want to know whether the same games come on a
          treadmill, or they have seen the name in a list of connected treadmills and want to know
          what it is. The answer is that Aviron, a Toronto company that started with gamified
          rowers, now sells three treadmills in the US — the folding Justice and Podium and the
          42% incline Summit — and has retired the Victory treadmill it launched in 2024 from its own
          store. This page works through the three machines, what they cost once a membership is
          included, what still works if you stop paying, the fine print on a warranty that is
          longer than almost anyone else's, and who would be better served by a different
          treadmill.
        </p>

        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">1. Does Aviron Make a Treadmill? The Short Answer</h2>
<p>
            <strong>Yes. As of 20 October 2026 Aviron sells three treadmills in the US, direct from
            avironactive.com: the Justice from $1,999, the Podium from $2,499 and the Summit from
            $2,999, each with a 16-inch screen at Aviron's sale prices.</strong> For a buyer who wants
            Aviron's games and will keep the membership, the Podium is the sensible default; the
            Justice is the choice for walkers and joggers under 300 lb who are watching the budget;
            and the Summit is for people who will really use a 42% climb.
          </p>
          <p>
            Three things are worth knowing before you read further. First, the treadmill most
            existing reviews describe, the Aviron Victory, is no longer on Aviron's US store: its
            product pages now redirect to the three-model shop page. Second, the 20-year warranty
            that Aviron puts at the top of every page only applies if you buy directly from Aviron
            and keep paying a monthly or annual membership; otherwise it is 10 years on the frame
            and drive motor and one year on everything else. Third, the membership costs less than
            Peloton's, iFIT's or Echelon's, and the treadmill does more without it than most
            subscription-led machines — but the games that are the reason to buy an Aviron are
            behind it.
          </p>
          <p>
            If what you actually want is any treadmill with an entertaining screen, our
            <a href="/best-smart-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">smart treadmill roundup</a>
            compares the main connected platforms side by side.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="lineup" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">2. The Three Aviron Treadmills: Justice, Podium and Summit</h2>
<p>
            Launch coverage of the three treadmills appeared from 12 August 2026, Aviron's launch
            post says production units began shipping in the second week of September, and its
            formal press release is dated 9 September 2026. The table gives Aviron's own figures from
            its product pages on 20 October 2026. The product cards below carry only the figures that
            an independent source also confirms.
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[560px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Aviron figure</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Justice</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Podium</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Summit</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Sale price, 16 in. screen</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$1,999 (reg. $2,599)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$2,499 (reg. $3,249)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$2,999 (reg. $3,999)</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Motor</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">3.5 CHP brushless</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">4.5 CHP brushless</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">4.5 CHP brushless</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Belt</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">20 x 59 in.</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">22 x 60 in.</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">22 x 61 in.</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Top speed</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">12.5 mph</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">14 mph</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">14 mph, limited by grade</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Grade</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">0-15%</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">0-18%</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">-6% to 42%</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Max user</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">300 lb, up to 6 ft 6 in</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">350 lb, up to 6 ft 7 in</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">350 lb, up to 6 ft 8 in</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Machine weight</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">251 lb</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">284 lb</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">364 lb</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">In use (L x W x H)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">80 x 34 x 66 in.</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">80 x 37 x 66 in.</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">67 x 37 x 71 in.</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Folded</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">53 x 34 x 68 in.</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">49 x 37 x 68 in.</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Does not fold</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Screens</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">16 or 22 in.</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">16, 22 or 27 in.</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">16, 22 or 27 in.</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">WalkDesk</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Compatible</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Compatible</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Not compatible</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <p>
            All three share a cushioned deck with eight shock absorbers (larger ones on the Summit),
            built-in heart-rate sensors, a three-speed fan, wireless phone charging, two cup holders,
            customisable speed shortcut keys and a pivoting touchscreen. Aviron's specification
            tables also list a 2-megapixel camera and a microphone on the screen, which is worth
            knowing if you would rather not have either facing a room in your home; ask Aviron how
            to disable them before you buy.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">What the motor figures mean</h3>
          <p>
            Aviron quotes continuous horsepower (CHP) and footnotes it as a laboratory figure
            measured on a dynamometer at sustained maximum output, adding that normal workouts draw
            less. A continuous rating is the more useful kind to compare, but brands do not all test
            the same way, so treat a 3.5 against a 4.5 as a broad step up in headroom rather than a
            precise comparison with another maker's number. The practical difference shows in the
            ratings around the motor: the 4.5 CHP models carry 50 lb more user weight and run 1.5
            mph faster.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Where the sources disagree</h3>
          <p>
            Garage Gym Reviews' Summit review gives the speed range as 0.5 to 14.5 mph in one table
            and 0 to 14 mph in another; Aviron says 14 mph. The same review describes the Podium's
            deck as longer than the Summit's, which neither Aviron's figures (60 against 61 inches)
            nor the review's own specification table supports. And the Summit's 67-inch overall
            length, which Aviron and Garage Gym Reviews both give, is unusually short for a frame
            carrying a 61-inch belt. We have used Aviron's figures in the table, but if a few inches
            decide whether the Summit fits, confirm the length with Aviron in writing.
          </p>
        </div>
